B. What I need from you (documents and metadata)
To complete your request exactly as specified, please provide one or more of the following:
1. The IPO prospectus file (PDF or text). If there are multiple prospectuses, provide the one most recent to the IPO (or identify which you want).
2. The company’s latest annual report (PDF or text). If you want multiple years, provide the most recent annual report plus any earlier ones you want included.
3. If documents are hosted online, direct URLs (publicly accessible links) to the prospectus and annual report PDFs or HTML pages.
4. Optional but helpful: the company name and stock exchange / ticker and IPO date (so I can attempt to locate public filings if you want me to fetch them).

C. If you want me to fetch the documents (my proposed approach)
If you want me to locate the filings myself, provide the company name and ticker and I will:
1. Search major sources (company investor relations site, SEC EDGAR for US SEC registrants, or the relevant exchange/Regulator filings if non-US).
2. Download the IPO prospectus (prospectus/registration statement such as S-1/ F-1/ prospectus supplements) and the latest annual report (20-F, 10-K, or local jurisdiction annual report).
3. Identify sections of interest: “Non-GAAP measures”, “Adjusted EBITDA”, “Selected financial information”, “Financial highlights”, “Reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA to EBITDA/operating profit/net income”, “Notes to the financial statements” and “Pro forma/Restatement notes”.
4. Extract and produce the deliverable described below.

D. Template and exact deliverable I will produce once I have the documents
For each document (prospectus or annual report) I will provide the following items exactly as you requested:

1) Document name
- e.g., “Prospectus dated DD MMM YYYY (Registration Statement No. X)” or “Annual Report 20XX (Form 20-F / 10-K)”.

2) Reporting periods for which adjusted EBITDA is presented
- e.g., “FY2023, FY2022, FY2021” or “Six months ended 30 Jun 2023; Year ended 31 Dec 2022”.

3) Adjusted EBITDA numerical values and units (with table references/pages)
- I will extract the exact numbers and units, for example:
  - “Adjusted EBITDA: FY2023: USD 45.2 million; FY2022: USD 38.9 million; FY2021: USD 29.7 million — Table: ‘Non-GAAP measures’, page 45.”
- I will include the original table title, table number or figure, and page number(s). I will copy the text or table snippet as displayed in the document.

4) Reconciliation to EBITDA/GAAP measures showing adjustments
- I will extract the reconciliation table that shows how adjusted EBITDA is derived from net income, operating profit, or EBITDA.
- I will list each adjustment and numeric amount, e.g.:
  - “Net loss (GAAP): (USD 12.4m)
     + Depreciation & amortisation: +USD 21.6m
     + Share-based payments: +USD 4.3m
     + M&A related costs: +USD 2.1m
     = Adjusted EBITDA: USD 15.6m”
- I will include the page/table reference and copy the reconciliation text/table.

5) Definition/explanation of adjusted EBITDA and any pro forma or restatement notes
- I will extract the company’s definition verbatim (e.g., “Adjusted EBITDA means net profit/(loss) before interest, taxes, depreciation, amortisation and excluding share-based compensation, restructure costs, and one-off items…”).
- I will capture any notes on pro forma adjustments or restatements, including whether the measure is presented on a pro forma basis or if historical figures were restated.

6) Reporting currency and rounding conventions
- I will extract the statement of reporting currency and any rounding notes (e.g., “All amounts are expressed in US$ thousands, except per share amounts; numbers may not sum due to rounding.”).

7) Auditor notes or restatement disclosures that affect historical figures
- I will extract any auditor statements, audit opinion references, or notes indicating adjustments/restatements to historical figures related to non-GAAP measures or adjusted EBITDA (e.g., “The historical adjusted EBITDA for FY2021 has been restated due to…”, or auditor emphasis of matter).
- I will include page references and the exact quoted text.

E. Deliverable format and sample extraction (example structure)
Once documents are provided, the output for each document will look like:

Document: IPO Prospectus dated DD MMM YYYY (page XX–YY)
1. Reporting periods: FY2023, FY2022, FY2021
2. Adjusted EBITDA values:
   - FY2023: USD XX,XXX (Table 12, page 45) — snippet: “Adjusted EBITDA (USD’000): 45,200”
   - FY2022: USD XX,XXX (Table 12, page 45)
3. Reconciliation to EBITDA/GAAP:
   - Table: “Reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA to net profit (loss)”, page 46 — full table extracted verbatim.
4. Definition: “For the purposes of this prospectus, Adjusted EBITDA means …” (quoted paragraph)
5. Currency & rounding: “All amounts are in US$ thousands, rounded to the nearest thousand.”
6. Auditors/restatements: “Note X — Restatement: See auditors’ report page Z: …”

(Repeat for annual report.)

F. If you want a narrower or broader depth
- Depth options:
  - Shallow: Extract only the adjusted EBITDA numbers and reporting periods.
  - Medium: Extract numbers plus reconciliations and definitions.
  - Deep (recommended): Extract full sections: financial highlights, non-GAAP measures, selected financial information, notes on adjusted EBITDA and pro forma adjustments, and any auditor commentary. I will also capture table images or verbatim text snippets.

G. Next steps (recommendation)
- Please upload or link the IPO prospectus and the latest annual report (PDFs or web links).
- Tell me whether you want me to attempt fetching public filings (and provide the company name/ticker).
- Indicate depth: shallow / medium / deep (I recommend deep for full compliance with your manager’s needs).

H. If you prefer, I can start by searching for the documents if you give me:
- Company name and ticker
- IPO date or IPO year (or the exchange where it listed)

Once I have the documents (or permission to fetch them), I will promptly extract the required fields, include page/table references and provide verbatim snippets and tables per your requested format.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Non-GAAP measure extraction can be sensitive to context: companies define adjusted EBITDA differently — some exclude stock-based compensation, others exclude certain non-recurring items, and some present pro forma adjustments for acquisitions or IPO-related transactions. I will therefore quote definitions verbatim and capture any footnotes that explain which items are included/excluded.
- Auditor notes can be in different places: the auditor’s report, notes to the financial statements, or a separate “critical accounting policies” section; I will search all these areas.
- If you plan to use the extracted figures in regulatory or investment materials, ensure you cross-check any restatements and auditor disclaimers that may affect comparability.

If you provide the documents or authorize me to retrieve them given a company name/ticker, I will proceed immediately and produce the full requested extraction in the exact structure you specified.
==================

