Observation:
Here is the final answer from your managed agent 'retriever_agent':
### 1. Task outcome (short version):
I do not have any documents loaded in the corpus. I cannot confirm or extract any IPO prospectus or Annual report information. To proceed I need you to upload or provide the specific documents (PDFs or direct URLs to filings) or plain text of those documents. See the exact list and preferred depth below.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
Current status
- No document corpus is available to me in this session. I attempted to search the provided corpus but found no IPO prospectus or Annual report files accessible.
- Because I cannot access external sites myself, I cannot fetch filings from EDGAR, SEDAR, company investor sites or other repositories.

What I need from you (exact files/links and formats)
Please provide the following for the company and reporting periods you want compared. For best results, supply both an IPO prospectus (the final prospectus / registration statement used at listing) and the latest Annual Report (full annual report / Form 20-F or 10-K or equivalent). For each document, either upload the PDF(s) directly here or paste URLs that point to the PDF file itself (not to a web page summary). Acceptable formats:
- PDF files (preferred) — full document PDFs of the IPO prospectus and Annual report.
- Plain text or Word documents containing the full text (acceptable).
- Direct URLs to the PDF files (acceptable). Do not send only a webpage link that requires navigation; a direct link to a PDF is best.

Preferred depth and guidance (choose one)
- Shallow (fast): I will search each document for the terms “adjusted EBITDA”, “adjusted EBITDA reconciliation”, “adjusted earnings”, and extract only the numeric adjusted EBITDA values, reporting periods, and page/table references.
  - Use this if you want a quick comparison across documents.
- Medium (recommended): I will extract:
  - Document name and citation (file name + page number)
  - All reporting periods for which adjusted EBITDA is shown (e.g., FY2023, FY2022, LTM, quarter)
  - Adjusted EBITDA numerical values with units and rounding (e.g., $123m, in thousands)
  - Exact page/table references for each figure
  - Any reconciliation tables showing adjustments from GAAP EBITDA/Net income to adjusted EBITDA (copied or summarized)
  - The definition/explanation of adjusted EBITDA as stated in the document (verbatim or near-verbatim)
  - Reporting currency and statement on rounding conventions
  - Any auditor notes, footnotes, or restatement disclosures affecting historical figures
  - I will produce a side-by-side comparison table of reported adjusted EBITDA across the IPO prospectus and Annual report and note any material differences in definitions or adjustments.
- Deep: Everything in Medium plus:
  - Extract and transcribe full reconciliation tables and all related footnotes
  - Highlight inconsistencies or wording differences that could materially affect comparability (e.g., items included/excluded differ)
  - Extract management discussion that explains one-offs, pro-forma adjustments, or pro forma EBITDA used in valuation
  - Flag any auditor commentary about non-GAAP measures, restatements, or scope of audit on adjusted measures

Exactly what to upload/provide (concise checklist)
- IPO prospectus (final prospectus/registration statement). Preferred: PDF of the final filed prospectus (Form S-1, F-1, F-3, Prospectus, offering circular, etc.).
- Latest Annual Report (full PDF). Preferred: the most recent fiscal year full annual report (Form 20-F, 10-K, or the company’s Annual Report PDF).
- If you have multiple prospectus versions or amended registration statements, include the final version used at listing and any amendments that materially change adjusted EBITDA disclosures.
- If the company reports adjusted EBITDA in investor presentation rather than the prospectus, include the investor presentation PDF as well.
- Optional but helpful: any restatement notices, auditors’ reports, or press releases discussing adjustments or restatements.

How I will search/extract once you provide files
- I will search for keywords: “adjusted EBITDA”, “adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization”, “EBITDA (adjusted)”, “reconciliation”, “non-GAAP”, “pro forma EBITDA”, “adjustments”, “restatement”, and currency/rounding statements.
- For each document I will deliver:
  - Document name and file citation (file name + page number).
  - Reporting periods for adjusted EBITDA (e.g., 2023, 2022, LTM).
  - Adjusted EBITDA numeric values with units (e.g., “$123 million” or “USD thousands”) and exact page/table references.
  - Copy or clear summary of the reconciliation table(s) showing adjustments and the line items adjusted.
  - The definition/explanation text of adjusted EBITDA as provided in the document.
  - Reporting currency and rounding convention statements.
  - Any auditor notes or restatement disclosures affecting historical figures (with page references).
  - A short comparability assessment highlighting whether definitions and adjustments differ between IPO prospectus and Annual report and whether historical figures seem restated or reconciled differently.

If documents are not available (what you must do now)
- Please upload the IPO prospectus PDF and the latest Annual Report PDF (or provide direct PDF URLs). If you can only upload one at a time, start with the Annual Report (it typically contains audited historicals) and then the IPO prospectus.
- Indicate whether you want Shallow, Medium (recommended), or Deep extraction.
- If you do not have the PDF but have links to webpages, provide direct PDF links or copy/paste the relevant PDF text into a message.

Format for your reply to me (copy-paste this to make it fastest)
- Files attached: [attach IPO_prospectus.pdf] [attach Annual_Report_YYYY.pdf]
- OR URLs: IPO prospectus PDF URL: [paste direct PDF URL]; Annual Report PDF URL: [paste direct PDF URL]
- Desired depth: Shallow / Medium / Deep
- (Optional) Company name and listing date or ticker: [Company / Ticker]

Limitations and note
- I will not fetch external filings for you; I can only search documents you provide.
- If the IPO prospectus or Annual report uses tables embedded as images (scans), text extraction may require OCR. If you expect scanned PDFs, let me know and I will perform OCR (this may add time).
- If documents include multiple currencies or restated figures, I will extract the currency statements and note any conversions.

Minimum viable input to proceed immediately
- At minimum, upload the latest Annual Report PDF. With that alone I can extract adjusted EBITDA figures and notes from the Annual Report. To compare with IPO prospectus, also upload the IPO prospectus PDF.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Common pitfalls I will watch for:
  - Different definitions of adjusted EBITDA across documents: companies often exclude IPO-related one-offs in prospectuses but not in annual reports, or vice versa.
  - Different reporting periods or pro forma adjustments in prospectuses (sometimes include pro forma periods to show run-rate).
  - Rounding and units (thousands vs. millions) — I will note stated rounding conventions and convert to a consistent unit if asked.
  - Auditor commentary: auditors typically do not audit non-GAAP measures but will include required reconciliations; any auditor restatement or emphasis paragraph in the audited financials will be flagged.
- If you want, once you upload documents I can produce:
  - A concise one-page comparison summary (adjusted EBITDA by period and source) and
  - A detailed appendix with extracted reconciliation tables and verbatim definitions.

Please upload the files or paste direct PDF links now and state the desired extraction depth (Shallow / Medium / Deep). Once I have the documents I will proceed and produce the requested outputs with page and table references.
==================

