### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
What I checked and why I cannot proceed:
- No document corpus was provided in your message history or attached. I therefore cannot verify presence of an IPO prospectus or the latest Annual Report, nor can I extract adjusted EBITDA numbers or related reconciliation/notes.
- To complete the task as requested I need access to the source files in PDF form (or direct PDF URLs). The instructions below specify exactly what to provide and what I will extract at each depth.

Exact files/links required (please provide any or all as applicable):
1. IPO prospectus PDF (direct file upload or direct PDF URL). Example filename or link: Company_Prospectus.pdf or https://www.example.com/prospectus.pdf
2. Latest Annual Report PDF (direct file upload or direct PDF URL). Example filename or link: Company_AnnualReport_2024.pdf or https://www.example.com/annualreport2024.pdf

If the company has additional investor presentation PDFs or interim reports and you want them scanned for adjusted EBITDA references, you can include:
3. Investor Presentation PDF(s)
4. Interim Financial Report PDFs (e.g., Q1/Q2 reports)

What I will extract when the files are provided:
- Document name exactly as provided.
- Whether adjusted EBITDA is presented in the document.
- Reporting periods for which adjusted EBITDA is presented (e.g., FY 2023, Q4 2023, LTM, 12 months ended 31 Dec 2023).
- Adjusted EBITDA numerical values, with units (e.g., USD million) and page and/or table references (e.g., p. 45, Table 5).
- Reconciliation tables showing adjustments from statutory EBITDA (or operating profit/net income) to adjusted EBITDA — I will extract the full table contents and note table title/number and page.
- Text definition/explanation of adjusted EBITDA (verbatim excerpt and location).
- Reporting currency (e.g., USD, EUR) and rounding conventions (e.g., figures presented in thousands, millions, or rounded to nearest million).
- Any auditor notes or restatement disclosures affecting historical figures (auditor opinion paragraph, subsequent events, restatement note references with page numbers).
- For deep extraction: I will also output extracted tables in a CSV-like format and highlight discrepancies or missing reconciliation items.

Recommended extraction depth (pick one):
- Shallow (fast, minimal): good if you only need to know whether adjusted EBITDA is present and the headline numbers. Output: yes/no, pages, headline values.
- Medium (default balance): includes reconciliation tables and definition text plus currency/rounding. Output: tables captured as text, page refs.
- Deep (most thorough): includes full table extraction in structured form, auditor/restatement notes, and cross-checks across documents. Output: structured data suitable for downstream processing.

Minimum metadata I will need if you cannot upload full PDFs:
- Exact URLs pointing to direct PDF files (ending with .pdf). Webpages that are HTML rather than direct PDF links may not be fully processed; direct PDF links are preferred.
- If providing only excerpts or screenshots, please indicate pages of interest.

Next steps for you (concise):
