2. Indicate extraction depth: shallow / medium / deep.
3. Optionally indicate any pages you want prioritized.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Common locations to find adjusted EBITDA in these documents: Management Discussion & Analysis (MD&A), “Non-GAAP Financial Measures” section, investor presentation appendix, financial highlights table, or note disclosures. Reconciliation tables are often in the MD&A or a separate “Non-GAAP measures” note.
- If the company uses multiple currencies, I will note the reporting currency per document and any translation methodology stated (e.g., translated at average or closing rate).
- If historical figures were restated, auditor or accounting policy notes (e.g., Note X – Restatements, or Auditor’s Report emphasis paragraphs) typically describe the impact and will be extracted.
- If you want, when you upload PDFs I can first run a quick index pass (shallow) to point you to pages with adjusted EBITDA, then perform a medium or deep extraction on the selected documents.

