Requested files (exactly what I need from you):
- IPO prospectus (PDF or direct PDF URL), e.g., "CompanyName_Prospectus.pdf" or https://...
- Latest Annual Report (full PDF or direct PDF URL), e.g., "CompanyName_AnnualReport_YYYY.pdf" or https://...
Optional but helpful:
- Any interim/quarterly reports referenced in those documents (PDFs or URLs).
- Any separate financial supplement or investor presentation (PDF/URL).

Extraction service options:
- Shallow extraction (quick): confirm presence of IPO prospectus and Annual Report; list pages/tables where "adjusted EBITDA" appears; capture top-line adjusted EBITDA values and the reporting periods; turnaround: ~1–2 hours per document.
- Medium extraction (recommended): everything in shallow plus transcription of reconciliation table(s), definition/explanation of adjusted EBITDA, reporting currency and rounding conventions, and page/table references; turnaround: ~3–6 hours per document.
- Deep extraction (comprehensive): everything in medium plus verification of numbers against financial statements, capture auditor notes/restatement disclosures affecting historical figures, produce CSV of adjusted EBITDA line items and adjustments with page/table references; turnaround: ~1–2 days per document.

If you supply the PDFs or direct PDF URLs, I will perform the chosen extraction level and return:
- For each document: document name, reporting periods for which adjusted EBITDA is presented, adjusted EBITDA numerical values with units and page/table references, reconciliation tables showing adjustments (copied/extracted), the definition/explanation of adjusted EBITDA as given, reporting currency and rounding conventions, and any auditor/restatement notes affecting historical figures.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
What I checked and why I cannot extract now:
- I received only the task instructions and no document corpus (no PDFs or URLs were attached or accessible). Without the actual files I cannot search for the terms “adjusted EBITDA”, cannot locate reconciliation tables, cannot read definitions, nor can I verify reporting currency, rounding, or auditor/restatement notes.

Exact items I will extract once you provide documents:
- Document identification:
  - Exact filename or URL and document title (as printed in cover/title page).
- Reporting periods:
  - All reporting periods (years/quarters) for which “adjusted EBITDA” is presented (e.g., FY2023, FY2022, H1 2024).
- Adjusted EBITDA values:
  - Numerical values with units (e.g., “US$ million”, “£000”), including any stated rounding convention (e.g., “rounded to nearest million”).
  - Page number and table/figure reference (e.g., “page 74, Table 5: Reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA”).
- Reconciliation tables:
  - Capture the full reconciliation table(s) showing adjustments from statutory measure (e.g., EBITDA or profit/(loss) from operations) to adjusted EBITDA, listing each adjustment (e.g., stock-based compensation, restructuring, M&A costs) with numeric amounts and references.
- Definition/explanation:
  - The company’s textual definition of “adjusted EBITDA” (verbatim), and any notes explaining why adjustments are made.
- Reporting currency and rounding:
  - Stated reporting currency for the financial statements and any rounding conventions affecting presented numbers.
- Auditor/restatement notes:
  - Any auditor comments, qualifications, or restatement disclosures that affect historical figures or adjustments (e.g., restated comparatives, prior period adjustments, audit opinion notes).
- Cross-checks:
  - If discrepancies exist between prospectus and Annual Report, I will flag them and provide page references.

What I will deliver in the final output:
- A concise summary per document and a short consolidated table of adjusted EBITDA by period and source (prospectus vs Annual Report), with page/table references.
- Extracted reconciliation table(s) as text or CSV (depending on chosen depth).
- Direct quotes of adjusted EBITDA definition and auditor/restatement notes.
- A clear statement if adjusted EBITDA is not defined or reconciliation missing.

Why the optional documents are helpful:
- Prospectus may include pro forma adjustments or non-GAAP measures that differ from Annual Report; having both PDFs allows me to reconcile differences.
- Financial supplements/investor presentations sometimes contain interim adjusted EBITDA figures or alternative reconciliations that clarify group reporting.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- If the company has multiple registrable entities or consolidated vs pro forma presentations (common in prospectuses), please indicate which legal entity or presentation you want prioritized.
- If you need machine-readable outputs (CSV/JSON) for ingestion, specify that when you upload files.
- If privacy/confidentiality is a concern, you can provide secure links (S3, Google Drive, OneDrive) or indicate any pages I should avoid.

Next step for you:
- Upload the IPO prospectus PDF and the latest Annual Report PDF (or provide direct PDF URLs) and tell me which extraction option you want (shallow/medium/deep). Once I have the files I will proceed and return the requested structured extraction.
